Description:
    Longitudinal microbiome studies often lose whole samples when a subject
    misses a visit or a library fails quality control. The affected
    subject-timepoint is then absent from the abundance table.
    TaxaTimeImpute estimates the missing values by modelling each taxon's
    abundance over time as a smooth curve and sharing information across
    subjects with Functional Principal Component Analysis. Sparse and
    irregularly sampled designs are supported. Imputed values can be reported
    with analytic or bootstrap confidence intervals. Functional-depth outlier
    screening and trajectory clustering are available as options. Input may be
    an abundance table, a SummarizedExperiment, or a TreeSummarizedExperiment.
